{"title":"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has integer side lengths and is divided into four rectangles, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The largest of these four rectangles is shaded and has a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. The smallest rectangle is striped and has a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cm. What is the perimeter, in cm, of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c352e9db5a7134ca93f9fecce8fe99b0d4e5889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d78aae1741ff43c6f40e2077f1ab67900cca2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce0501dff8a93818a4e5d9ecc570d8ab6472e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec781a0e6836ea5e030a44927477cfd5560fecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the width of the shaded rectangle, the height of the shaded rectangle, the width of the striped rectangle, and the height of the striped rectangle, respectively.\n</p><p>From the perimeters of the striped and shaded rectangles, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27a4a920ec43689ef2a7524e8c73a37d7b014e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w_1 + 2h_1 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797d567259806ac37113e64f7c923c78095c7b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w_2 + 2h_2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We also can realize that the height of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is just the sum of the heights of the shaded and striped rectangles because opposite sides of rectangles are equal. Similarly, the width of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is just the sum of the widths of the shaded and stripes rectangles.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the perimeter of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. This means that we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88e5582caa77c8819fbd4011f50294bca75dc656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(w_1 + w_2) + 2(h_1 + h_2) = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b039effe8112809b8bb2a33c24791cf3d6cb104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2w_1 + 2h_1 + 2w_2 + 2h_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f27a4a920ec43689ef2a7524e8c73a37d7b014e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w_1 + 2h_1 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797d567259806ac37113e64f7c923c78095c7b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2w_2 + 2h_2 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"17\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afb650b1228980c9e5b68c146730245fb9c09f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 28 + 12 = \\boxed{40}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"148\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC\">2024 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CE